@startuml
title UC05 - independent consumption debit (REVIEW)
autonumber
actor "Authorized caller" as C
participant "Debit service" as S
participant "Operation outcomes" as O
participant "Specified account" as A
participant "Subscription / current cycle" as P
participant "Financial history" as L
C -> S : requestId, subscriber, account, amount, package/cycle
S -> O : resolve caller + UC05 + ID / canonical content
alt replay / conflict / PROCESSING
 O --> S : saved outcome / conflict / in progress
 S --> C : no new effect
else new operation
 group one consistent debit responsibility
  S -> A : coordinate specified account; verify owner and DEBIT permission
  S -> P : coordinate subscriber-owned root / cycle
  S -> A : AFTER all account/root/cycle coordination take fresh DB checkedAt
  S -> P : recheck cycle [start,end) and account expiry at this checkedAt
  alt no effective package / future or expired cycle / account expired
   S -> O : FAILED, no monetary effect
  else valid package and account
   S -> A : verify amount and sufficient balance
   alt insufficient funds
    A --> S : reject; no fallback/pooling
    S -> O : terminal FAILED, unchanged balance
   else enough funds
    S -> A : subtract exactly amount, never negative
    S -> L : SERVICE_CONSUMPTION, one cycle, recordedAt, balances
    S -> O : SUCCEEDED
   end
  end
 end
 S --> C : committed outcome
end
note over A,L
 Concurrent debit/credit preserves balance/ledger consistency.
 A fee inside UC02/renewal is not another UC05 API call/TPS.
 Timeout means outcome unknown to caller: lookup or retry same ID.
end note
@enduml
